# The image needs exactly two things: the Go server source and the exported web
# client. Everything else in this repo is either build input that already got
# turned into one of those two, or has no business on a server.
#
# Without this the whole 141MB working tree is uploaded to the builder on every
# deploy, most of it the Godot project the web export was made *from*.
*
!server/
!build/web/

# The export is a build artifact, so the .gz files sit next to their originals
# rather than in git (see .gitignore). They must reach the image: the server
# serves them to any client that accepts gzip, and without them every first
# load is 46MB instead of 17.7MB.
!build/web/**

# Never ship credentials or local state, even by accident.
**/.env
**/*.pem
**/.DS_Store
